    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents asset removal cost net of salvage.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Restricted cash is included in line 86, relating to Net Increase (Decrease) in Cash and Cash Equivalents, line 88, Cash and Cash Equivalents at Beginning of Period, and line 90, Cash and Cash Equivalents at End of Period.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Restricted cash is included in line 86, relating to Net Increase (Decrease) in Cash and Cash Equivalents, line 88, Cash and Cash Equivalents at Beginning of Period, and line 90, Cash and Cash Equivalents at End of Period.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period of 31 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ECCRA rider is an annual filing. A portion of these costs are recovered in base rates and this portion is being amortized over a period of 10 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period of 10 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period of 10 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortized over the life of the assets.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period of 10 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">OSS Margin rider is an annual filing. Balance has flipped to a credit position and is now included on Page 278.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Costs associated with Cause No. 45911 will be amoritzed over 4 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">A portion of this regulatory asset is recovered in base rates and amortized over the average life of the assets or 4 years and a portion being recovered in a future base rate case so amortization period has not yet been determined. The remainder relates to the annual TDSIC rider rate filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">DSM Rider is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is 4 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This is a balancing account where major storm costs are deferred and an amount is collected in base rates. AES Indiana is currently recovering $159,000 monthly in base rates that is applied against this regulatory asset. AES Indiana is also crediting customers $168,000 in base rates for prior over collection of storm costs. This is applied to the regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Investment is recovered in the annual ECCRA rider filing. Amortization period period will be over the life of the solar project.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Investment is recovered in the annual ECCRA rider filing. Amortization period period will be over the life of the project.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel Adjustment Charge is a quarterly filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Investment is recovered in the annual ECCRA rider filing. Amortization period period will be over the life of the project.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Capacity Rider is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">A portion is being amortized over the estimated remaining useful life of the asset. Carrying costs, O&amp;M, and depreciation are included in the ECCRA filing and are amortized over the remaining useful life of the project except for O&amp;M which is amortized over twelve months.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is 4 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Costs will be recovered in a future base rate case. Amortization period is not yet determined.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">RTO is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization will begin once assets are retired. Amortization rates are based on depreciation rates approved in Cause No. 45911. Amortization of Pete 3 began in February 2026.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Investment will be recovered in the annual ECCRA rider filing. Amortization period period will be over the life of the project.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is 12 months and will begin once updated transmission formula rates are implemented.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Green Power Rider is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period of ITC credits and allowance deferral is twelve months via in the annual ECCRA filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Vegetation management costs are collected in base rates but AES Indiana is required to reflect a lialibity for any underspend since the last base rate implementaiton. The account acts like a balancing account where the liability would be adjusted monthly as additional spend is incurred until there is no longer a liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is 12 months and will begin once updated transmission formula rates are implemented.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Long-Term Firm and Short-Term Firm Point-to-Point Service under Schedule 7 of the MISO FERC Electric Tariff and Non-Firm Point-to-Point Service under Schedule 8 of the MISO FERC Electric Tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Midcontinent Independent System Operator, Inc. - FERC Electric Tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All revenue is collected by MISO and distributed to Indianapolis Power &amp; Light Company d/b/a AES Indiana, therefore, billing demand information is not available.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All revenue is collected by MISO and distributed to Indianapolis Power &amp; Light Company d/b/a AES Indiana, therefore, transfer of energy information is not available.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Invoices from MISO do not include megawatt hours.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transmission Charges and Credits received by MISO.</link:footnote>
